McKinsey Global Institute estimates AI could add $13–22 trillion to global GDP annually by 2030 through automation of knowledge work, personalisation, and process optimisation.
AI-powered code generation tools (GitHub Copilot) increase developer productivity by 55% in controlled studies — among the largest measured productivity improvements in the history of software engineering.
Precision agriculture AI (crop yield prediction, disease detection, irrigation optimisation) is increasing farm yields by 10–20% while reducing water and fertiliser use, addressing food security at scale.
Every major industrial economy that has adopted automation at scale (Japan, South Korea, Germany) has lower unemployment and higher wages than less automated economies — robots complement rather than replace workers at the macro level.
